dtk-rs workspace packaging
==========================

This source package builds two Rust source packages from one Cargo workspace:
librust-dtk-sys-dev contains the low-level cxx bridge and C++ shim, while
librust-dtk-dev contains the safe wrapper crate and depends on the former.

Cargo requires a version for a path dependency before it can create a crate
archive.  1001_packageable-manifest.patch adds that version without changing
workspace development, where the path continues to take precedence.

Under Debian's --as-needed linker flags, the generated static shim must appear
before the Qt6 and DTK6 shared libraries which resolve its symbols.
1002_link-static-shim-first.patch delays pkg-config's link metadata until after
cxx-build has emitted the dtkshim link directive.

dtk-sys embeds a generated static library named dtkshim into downstream Rust
binaries.  2001_dh-cargo-built-using.patch identifies the corresponding MIT
licensed source directory for dh-rust.  This lets application packages produce
correct Built-Using metadata instead of failing during dh_auto_install.

The native DTK6, Qt6, pkg-config and moc dependencies are runtime dependencies
of librust-dtk-sys-dev because that package ships source code whose build.rs is
executed while compiling each downstream application.

Rust dependencies are consumed from /usr/share/cargo/registry.  Do not add a
vendored Cargo registry to this source package; missing crates should be
packaged independently.

dtk-sys uses Rust edition 2024.  cxx and cxx-build 1.0.192 are the oldest
versions validated for this package; the older 1.0.87 code generator emits
extern blocks which Rust 2024 rejects.  Both the source and binary dependency
fields therefore enforce the validated lower bound.
